            <ArticleTitle>Subchondral osteoid osteoma of the glenoid.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S79-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12306-009-0011-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteoid osteoma of the scapula is a rare benign lesion. This is a case report of a subchondral osteoid osteoma that involved the anterior rim of glenoid. Surgical approach in this atypical area may seem difficult. The excision of the lesion and grafting was performed by a deltopectoral approach. One year after the surgery, the patient remains pain free and has full range of motion with no recurrence of the tumour.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
